{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3269","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3269","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3269\",\"parent_revision\":\"8f7d365b5eb61a339d5551f0ad4bae51ae53ee61\",\"root_revision\":\"cb01777051ac1d191b313791aeed252f2c70112a0f7dcc199b58052f5963ce06\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe feasibility gate in `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md` (Criterion 3 \u2014 blast radius check) treats blast radius as a flat sum of Impact Radius rows across all categories, with a fixed \\\"over 20 systems\\\" BLOCKED threshold. This produced a BLOCKED result while working backlog item #3151 in this session, despite that item having RT-ICA verdict READY and Design Intent verdict MISSION_ALIGNED: the count (~67) mixed 2 structural/high-risk files with ~43 already-itemized, near-identical, low-risk prose edits, and the flat count did not distinguish between them.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: The optional `pattern:` row annotation (intended so the gate can re-verify a count live via `rg -l '<pattern>' | wc -l` against staleness) is agent-discretionary \u2014 nothing requires impact-analyst to add it \u2014 and even when present, measures string-match occurrence rather than actual change impact, so it may not reliably signal real blast-radius drift.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: The BLOCKED Output Contract's generic \\\"To retry: re-groom the item... then re-run\\\" footer is intended for Criterion 1 (missing `suggested_location`) and the `STALE_GROOM` branch of Criterion 3 (a live-vs-manual count divergence), where re-grooming can genuinely supply missing or refreshed data. It also fires for the flat \\\">20 systems\\\" branch of Criterion 3, even when the count was freshly produced in the same session and is not stale \u2014 in that case re-grooming would not change the outcome, so the retry advice does not resolve that specific block.\\n\\nImpact: a well-groomed, RT-ICA-ready, mission-aligned item stops at the feasibility gate with retry advice that does not apply to the branch that fired, requiring a human to recognize this and improvise (e.g., manually deciding to split the item into a structural sub-plan and a mechanical sweep sub-plan) rather than the gate itself surfacing that option.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: proposed directions for grooming/planning to evaluate, not requirements \u2014 (1) weight blast radius by category rather than a flat sum, so code producers/consumers count toward the risk threshold while documentation/agent-instruction prose (especially rows the impact-analyst already itemized individually) counts separately against a much looser threshold or not at all; (2) reconsider the `pattern:`/live-recount mechanism \u2014 either require it whenever an analyst asserts an aggregate \\\"N remaining files\\\" bucket, or drop the live-recount step and trust a groom that ran in the same session; (3) split the single BLOCKED Output Contract into two templates \u2014 one for \\\"data is stale/incomplete, re-run X\\\" (Criteria 1, 2, and STALE_GROOM), and one for \\\"scope is large but well-understood, human must confirm or split\\\" (the flat >20 branch) \u2014 since the correct next action differs between them.\\n\\nRelated: #1135 (staleness detection for Step 3.1) addresses a different mechanism \u2014 drift between groom date and re-use \u2014 not this item's concern (risk-weighting and threshold design within Criterion 3 itself).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-28, while running /dh:work-backlog-item work on #3151 and hitting the feasibility gate's blast-radius block\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"48fb72c8a7225fb24ea8474b15d9fd0a5f5e4859240224752c30c9715b7ac021\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABReqiKg\"}"}